            <ArticleTitle>Non-cardiac chest pain: a clinical assessment tool.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>296-300</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/hmed.2015.76.5.296</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A simple clinical approach to patients presenting with chest pain is outlined, which is easily taught and can be quickly applied. This approach was demonstrated in a large cohort of patients and this article discusses the characteristics of the various diagnostic sub-groups.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
